    <string name="guide_title">OBD-II Hardware &amp; GM GMLAN Buying Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_recommended_mxplus">1. Recommended: OBDLink MX+ (STN2255 Chip)</string>
    <string name="guide_mxplus_description">A high-end STN interface is recommended for advanced GM diagnostics. Physical SW-CAN support depends on the exact adapter model and does not by itself guarantee BCM, IPC or SDM access; protocols and identifiers must be validated for the VIN.</string>
    <string name="guide_hscan_alternative">2. HS-CAN Alternative: vLinker MC+ / OBDLink LX</string>
    <string name="guide_vlinker_description">High-throughput reliability on powertrain/ABS HS-CAN (500 kbps). The vLinker MC+ also supports GMLAN SW-CAN.</string>
    <string name="guide_clone_limitations">3. Limitations of Generic ELM327 v2.1 Clones</string>
    <string name="guide_clone_description">Low-cost blue/mini ELM327 clones lack physical transceivers on Pin 1 (SW-CAN), suffer from truncated RX buffers, and often fail extended CAN header addressing. Module access always depends on vehicle equipment, adapter hardware, and supported protocols.</string>
